    "body": "- Add `run` helper script and `.dockerignore` files.\r\n- Update `build_dependencies.sh` to include GTest so we can run unit tests on Windows.\n\n<!-- Reviewable:start -->\n- - -\nThis change is [<img src=\"https://reviewable.io/review_button.svg\" height=\"34\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"Reviewable\"/>](https://reviewable.io/reviews/TokTok/c-toxcore/2980)\n<!-- Reviewable:end -->\n",
    "changed_files": 8,
    "closed_at": "2026-01-17T12:37:46Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": ">2 separate changes, but only 1 commit\r\n\r\n[Why does iphy always do this?](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-add#Documentation/git-add.txt--p)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDon't really get the obsession with having Dockerfiles work relative to the repository root, this makes Dockerfile no longer portable anymore, since it assumes specific directory structure in the levels above it, but whatever, while not my preference, it also works, I guess. We had to assume it for the cygwin build in:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/TokTok/c-toxcore/blob/ed37616249c703e3d8e319b1300aead8e1de22f0/other/docker/windows/build_toxcore.sh#L36-L43\r\n\r\nbefore, but this one instance aside, it was portable.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n>-   Update `build_dependencies.sh` to include GTest so we can run unit tests on Windows.\r\n\r\nI see there were some new tests added? Network simulator and such? That's cool.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"emoji\" title=\":lgtm_strong:\" alt=\":lgtm_strong:\" align=\"absmiddle\" src=\"https://reviewable.io/lgtm_strong.png\" height=\"20\" width=\"61\"/>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- Sent from Reviewable.io -->\r\n",
